WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.010
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:09.080
Today I am going to explain an American comedy
fantasy film called “Click.”

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.450
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:16.390
Watch out and take care!

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:22.390
The movie starts as we see the main protagonist,
Michael Newman, who is an architect by profession.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:28.720
He lives with his family of four which include
his wife Donna and two children, Ben and Samantha.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:35.079
Michael’s heavy-handed boss John Ammer makes
him work more than necessary and as a result,

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:37.650
Michael often ends up ignoring his family.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:41.840
Despite all this, Michael finds a lot of joy
out of the little time he gets to spend with

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.730
his children like when he watches Dragon Tales
with them before leaving for work.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:52.239
One day at work, John offers Michael a once
in a lifetime opportunity to design a luxury

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:54.690
hotel for a Japanese conglomerate.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:01:00.050
He also promises Michael a promotion if he
is able to seal the contract.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:04.949
Michael is elated by the proposition but realizes
that he has to go camping with his family.

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:08.030
Later, he also misses Ben’s swimming race.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.520
When Michael reaches the school, he is greeted
by Ben’s swimming teacher Bill with whom

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.950
Ben seems to have a good friendship.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:19.410
He instantly becomes jealous as he isn’t
able to spend much time with his son.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.920
Hence, he makes fun of Bill’s red speedo.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.549
As the family gathers at the fourth of July
fireworks, Michael spends all his time on

00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:30.950
the phone with his boss, which begins to annoy
Michael’s mother Trudy.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:36.020
She complains that Michael will die early
if he continues to overwork and eat junk food.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:41.620
As Michael is occupied on the phone, his father
Ted entertains the kids with his quarter trick.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:46.020
Fascinated by the trick, Ben and Samantha
ask their grandfather how he managed to bend

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.860
the coin but Ted responds that “a magician
never reveals his secrets”.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:56.360
Ted further adds that even the “big boy”
Michael hasn’t been able to decode his secret.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:09.259
Later at home, an argument erupts when Michael
tells Donna to postpone the camping trip.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:14.150
He eventually calms her down and starts his
project research by watching an Asian architecture

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.150
documentary.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.459
However, he hurts himself when he accidentally
mistakes Ben’s helicopter remote for the

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:20.940
TV remote.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.480
Tired of always mixing up the remotes, Michael
heads out to the supermarket to buy a universal

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.190
remote control.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.260
Michael enters the retail store Bed Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.959
He looks everywhere for the remote but doesn’t
find it.

00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:36.190
A tired Michael then collapses on a bed.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.550
When he turns around, he spots a section of
the store called “Beyond”.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:45.780
When he gets inside to inspect, he is welcomed
by a mysterious man named Morty.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.400
Michael begins to explain about his situation
to Morty, who then takes Micahel to a large

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.190
warehouse called “Way Beyond”.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:56.720
Morty then grabs a weird looking remote and
offers it to Michael for free.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.620
Morty tells Michael that the remote will program
itself when he points and clicks the buttons.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:07.320
A confused Michael inquires why he is being
given the remote for free, to which Morty

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.670
responds that “Good guys need a break every
once in a while”.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:16.269
As Michale prepares to leave, he is also told
that the item is ‘non refundable.’

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:20.599
After Michael reaches home, he continues watching
the documentary and begins working on the

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:21.890
project design.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:25.760
However, he is soon disturbed by his dog Sundance.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.560
The poor doggo wants a break outside so he
continues to bark.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:34.390
A furious Michael then points the remote at
Sundance and presses the volume down button

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:38.629
repeatedly, while shouting at the dog to remain
silent for five minutes.

00:03:38.629 --> 00:03:48.350
Astonishingly, the dog becomes mute but Michael
dismisses it as he thinks it's just a hallucination.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:52.340
After Michael takes Sundance out, he starts
getting frustrated again as the dog takes

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.159
really long to find a spot to relieve himself.

00:03:55.159 --> 00:03:59.170
So he points the remote at the dog again,
while pressing fast forward.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:03.950
Just like the last time, the trick works,
as the remote fastracks sundance, who quickly

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:07.000
finishes his work and gets back inside.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.250
Michael is astonished and finally believes
the power of the universal remote.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:15.319
He finds out that the remote can be used to
control real life.

00:04:15.319 --> 00:04:19.289
The following day, Michael uses the remote
to look into his past life.

00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:23.599
He gets emotional when he sees his little
self play football with his friends at lake

00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:24.599
Winnipesaukee.

00:04:24.599 --> 00:04:30.099
Meanwhile, Morty gives Michael his phone number
in case he has any questions about the remote.

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:35.249
Michael uses the remote to fast forward through
family dinner, arguments and even intercourse.

00:04:35.249 --> 00:04:38.789
After fast-forwarding the intercourse, Michael
is surprised to learn that he “climaxed”

00:04:38.789 --> 00:04:42.569
very quickly, and couldn’t pleasure Donna
like he normally used to.

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:46.520
He also learns that he doesn’t remember
the conversations he had or commitments he

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.400
made during the dinner.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.259
Michael calls Morty and demands an explanation
for it.

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:55.199
Morty says that during fast forward, his body
is on "auto-pilot".

00:04:55.199 --> 00:05:00.259
This means that he is going through the motions
of everyday life but his mind skips ahead.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:04.599
In this way, while Michael seems to live a
normal life, he doesn’t remember any of

00:05:04.599 --> 00:05:05.599
it.

00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:09.969
After this revelation, Michael uses the remote
to fast forward through undesirable things

00:05:09.969 --> 00:05:13.270
like sickness, cold showers, and traffic.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:18.969
He also presents the design he made on auto-pilot
mode to the Japanese businessman Mr. Watsuhita.

00:05:18.969 --> 00:05:24.369
The meeting seems to be going great but Michael’s
over excited boss John unintentionally mocks

00:05:24.369 --> 00:05:28.470
Japan’s iconic baseball players, mistaking
their name for Asian dishes.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:33.370
This prompts Mr. Watsushita to excuse himself
and have a private conversation with his team.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:38.720
A nervous Michael tries to overhear Watsuhita's
conversation, but can't understand any of

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.720
it.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.539
So, he uses the remote to translate their
conversation into English and turn up their

00:05:43.539 --> 00:05:44.539
volume.

00:05:44.539 --> 00:05:48.809
The trick works, and it reveals that the Japanese
team disliked Michael's design, commenting

00:05:48.809 --> 00:05:53.039
that it must have been made after watching
a bad documentary on Asian architecture.

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:58.139
They wanted more rooms to maximize their profits
and not a stupid river in the lobby.

00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:02.439
Mr. Watsuhita then orders his team to end
the meeting so that they can have Jello shots

00:06:02.439 --> 00:06:06.000
at America’s greatest cultural achievement:
TGI Friday’s.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.789
However, when Mr. Watsuhita approaches Michael
to wrap up, he uses the overheard conversation

00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:13.590
to win over the businessman.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:20.400
He rips his failed design and offers to make
a new one to incorporate more rooms to maximise

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.189
profits.

00:06:22.189 --> 00:06:28.860
A delighted Mr. Watsuhita finally grants the
contract to Michael’s company.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:33.809
Later at home, a super elated Michael buys
gifts for his wife and children.

00:06:33.809 --> 00:06:38.210
When Donna inquires about the reason for Michael's
joy, he reveals that John has promoted him

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.529
to a partnership.

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:41.539
Donna jumps in excitement.

00:06:41.539 --> 00:06:46.080
However, the excitement turns into disappointment
the next day, when Michael learns that he

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.479
hasn’t been promoted.

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:51.669
As a matter of fact, he won’t be promoted
until he prepares the construction plan for

00:06:51.669 --> 00:06:57.509
the hotel and gets Mr. Watsuhita's commitment,
which will take him several months.

00:06:57.509 --> 00:07:05.240
Devastated by the news, Michael uses the remote
to pause John and fart in his mouth.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:09.560
In the next scene, Michael plans on using
the remote to fast forward to the time he

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.810
finishes the Watsuhita project.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:16.029
When he seeks Morty’s advice, Morty reminds
Michael about the leprechaun from a cereal

00:07:16.029 --> 00:07:17.029
advertisement.

00:07:17.029 --> 00:07:21.479
The leprechaun always chases a pot of gold
at the end of the rainbow but when he finally

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:24.940
gets there, he realises it is just cornflakes.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.679
Michael doesn’t understand the metaphor
but nevertheless suspends his plans to use

00:07:28.679 --> 00:07:29.679
the remote.

00:07:29.679 --> 00:07:34.710
At home, Michael is still frustrated over
his promotion and takes it out on his children.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:40.180
The kids start crying when Michael makes fun
of their pizza and pickles.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.289
He then has an argument with Donna.

00:07:42.289 --> 00:07:44.830
Later, Michael realises his mistake.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:49.319
He is annoyed by his actions so he finally
decides to use the remote to skip ahead to

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:53.240
his promotion and finds himself at his promotion
party.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.789
He finds out that it took John a whole year
to promote him.

00:07:56.789 --> 00:08:01.719
During this time, Donna and Michael’s relations
started to get strained and they entered marriage

00:08:01.719 --> 00:08:02.819
counseling.

00:08:02.819 --> 00:08:08.399
Ben and Samantha have matured and no longer
watch the Dragon tales cartoon.

00:08:08.399 --> 00:08:12.089
He also learns that Sundance has passed away.

00:08:12.089 --> 00:08:16.159
Michael breaks down and regrets not letting
his late dog hump his leg.

00:08:16.159 --> 00:08:19.399
This confuses Donna but she consoles him anyway.

00:08:19.399 --> 00:08:23.189
Michael promises Donna that he will change
and become a better man for her.

00:08:23.189 --> 00:08:25.800
He asks her to not leave him.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.930
Michael and Donna make out but the remote
automatically fast forwards to the end of

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.360
the intercourse.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.870
Michael again finds an unsatisfied Donna lying
next to him on bed.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:40.130
He is puzzled by the remote automatically
skipping time without him pressing any buttons.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:45.230
He then contacts Morty, who reveals that the
remote is now using its memory to execute

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.420
Michael’s preferences.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.459
That’s google way ahead of its time!

00:08:49.459 --> 00:08:54.009
Michael fast forwarded through an entire year
and that accounted for a lot of intercourse

00:08:54.009 --> 00:08:55.009
skipped.

00:08:55.009 --> 00:08:59.480
Now each time he tries having intercourse
or involves in events like showering, driving

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:04.279
through traffic, arguing, and being sick,
the remote is going to fast forward on its

00:09:04.279 --> 00:09:05.279
own.

00:09:05.279 --> 00:09:09.480
Hearing this, Michael regrets having ever
used the remote and returns the remote to

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.990
Morty but it automatically reappears in his
hand.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:17.260
He then makes several attempts to discard
and destroy the remote but it reappears each

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.339
time.

00:09:18.339 --> 00:09:22.740
The next day, Michael goes to office on a
bicycle without showering so that he can avoid

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.149
the time being automatically fast forwarded.

00:09:25.149 --> 00:09:29.420
There, John tells him about his plans to retire
and travel to Morocco.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:33.589
John’s retirement would make Michael the
new head of the International Division at

00:09:33.589 --> 00:09:34.699
the firm.

00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:39.060
While Michael is stunned by his promotion
to such a high post, John exclaims that every

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.990
account Michael has worked on has turned into
gold.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:46.560
John also comments that he wouldn’t be surprised
if one day Michael ended up being their company's

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.670
CEO.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:55.180
Suddenly, Michael is fast-forwarded ten years
into the future, where he is wealthy, but

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:56.589
morbidly obese.

00:09:56.589 --> 00:10:00.310
He quickly returns home to find that Ben and
Samantha are grown up teenagers.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:05.440
Ben too has become an obese guy much like
himself while Samantha has started dating

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.440
someone.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:11.670
He also learns that Donna has divorced him
and is dating Ben’s swimming teacher Bill.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:15.029
Enraged by their relationship, Michael attacks
Bill.

00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:19.339
An argument ensues and the family dog jumps
on Michael, causing him to knock his head

00:10:19.339 --> 00:10:21.790
on the wall and fall unconscious.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.630
After six long years, Michael finally gains
consciousness.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:30.519
Donna is there by his side, who reveals that
after he went into a coma, a CAT scan found

00:10:30.519 --> 00:10:34.750
cancer in his body, so he had to undergo treatment
for years.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:37.480
After beating cancer, he had a heart attack
too.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:42.839
However, Michael is no longer fat as a result
of having undergone liposuction to save his

00:10:42.839 --> 00:10:43.839
life.

00:10:43.839 --> 00:10:48.370
Later at the firm, Michael meets an adult
Ben, who has surprisingly lost a lot of weight

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.000
working out with Donna’s husband Bill.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.300
Michael offers to take Ben, Samantha, and
their grandparents out for an ice cream but

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:58.689
Ben reveals that grandpa Ted has already died.

00:10:58.689 --> 00:11:03.470
This devastates Michael who breaks into tears
and visits Ted’s grave.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.510
Michael then uses the remote to re-experience
the time when he last saw his dad.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:12.350
Michael sees that Ted dropped by his office
and offered to take Ben and him out for dinner.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:17.310
But an autopilot Michael rejected the offer
without even looking at the old man.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:21.620
Ted continued to insist and offered to show
Michael his favorite childhood quarter trick

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:25.949
but an agitated Michael yelled at his father,
while revealing that he had always known the

00:11:25.949 --> 00:11:27.410
secret to the trick.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:31.990
The poor old man then apologized and left
with tears in his eyes.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:34.290
Michael gets filled with shame and guilt.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:38.980
Morty then appears and apologises for taking
his father away, admitting that he is the

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:39.980
Angel of Death.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:43.779
Michael gets angry by the revelation and attacks
Morty.

00:11:43.779 --> 00:11:47.970
However, Morty disappears into thin air and
reappears behind him.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:52.600
Frightened, Michael asks the remote to take
him to a "good place" whereupon the remote

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.550
fast-forwards him several more years in the
future to Ben's wedding.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:12:00.980
At the wedding, Michael is elated to see his
mother and gives her a long kiss.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:08.709
He also meets an all grown 
up Samantha.

00:12:08.709 --> 00:12:13.139
Michael hears her calling Bill “dad” and
suffers from a heart attack, unable to bear

00:12:13.139 --> 00:12:16.350
the pain of being replaced even as a father.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:20.350
He wakes in the hospital that night with Ben
and Samantha by his side.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:24.459
Before Ben and Samantha are escorted out by
the nurse, Michael finds out that Ben is skipping

00:12:24.459 --> 00:12:26.650
his honeymoon because of a business deal.

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:30.980
Fearing that Ben might make the same mistakes
he made, Michael gathers the last of his strength

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.689
to follow them out of the hospital.

00:12:32.689 --> 00:12:38.300
However, his body gives out and he collapses
onto the ground, with his family around him.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:43.889
In a very low voice, he suggests Ben to always
put family first and apologises to Samantha

00:12:43.889 --> 00:12:45.800
for not being there for her.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:49.939
Michael then tells Donna that he will always
love her and passes away.

00:12:49.939 --> 00:12:53.490
Suddenly, Michael reawakens in Bed Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:57.649
He is elated to learn that everything was
just a dream.

00:12:57.649 --> 00:13:02.269
Outside, he is overjoyed to see his “crappy,
mediocre, middle class” car.

00:13:02.269 --> 00:13:07.699
After he reaches home, he embraces his family
and promises to spend more time with them.

00:13:07.699 --> 00:13:11.880
Just then, he then finds the remote on the
counter along with a note from Morty, which

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:16.509
says that he has been given a second chance
as "Good guys need a break."

00:13:16.509 --> 00:13:19.589
Morty also hopes that Michael will do the
right thing this time.

00:13:19.589 --> 00:13:24.550
The movie ends as Michael throws the remote
in the trash and gets delighted as this time,

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:47.559
it does not reappear.

